From 5ac30bf934c01d7bfe8f9464dcfd85c0fb7d9e09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:04:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] config: Adds pointer acceleration, double-click time and
 sloppy focus.

Settings Window Maker's preferences offer, which wlmaker lacked:

 - 'Mouse' section, for all pointer devices: libinput's acceleration speed
   ('AccelSpeed', -1.0 to 1.0) and profile ('AccelProfile', Adaptive or
   Flat). Window Maker sets the speed with 'xset m'. Without the section,
   libinput's defaults apply.
 - 'Mouse.DoubleClickTime': The time between the clicks of a double-click on
   the title bar (which shades the window), fixed at 300 ms before. Set via
   wlmtk_titlebar_set_double_click_msec().
 - 'FocusMode': Click (the default), or Sloppy: A window gets activated (not
   raised) when the pointer enters it, like Window Maker's 'sloppy' focus.
   The desktop gets wlmtk_desktop_set_focus_follows_pointer().

'WindowPlacement', 'FocusMode' and the double-click time are applied by
wlmaker_server_configure_desktop().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
